1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:01,899
After ten years of war,

2
00:00:01,899 --> 00:00:03,899
the Greeks leave their enemy a giant

3
00:00:03,899 --> 00:00:06,019
wooden horse, and sail home.

4
00:00:06,019 --> 00:00:07,719
The Trojans rush to the beach.

5
00:00:07,719 --> 00:00:08,220
No army.

6
00:00:08,220 --> 00:00:08,779
No ships.

7
00:00:08,779 --> 00:00:09,740
Just a horse.

8
00:00:09,740 --> 00:00:11,939
A priest named Laocoön hurls a spear

9
00:00:11,939 --> 00:00:14,580
into its side, and it sounds… hollow.

10
00:00:14,830 --> 00:00:16,609
Beware of Greeks bearing gifts!

11
00:00:16,609 --> 00:00:18,030
Then they find one Greek hiding in

12
00:00:18,030 --> 00:00:19,429
the reeds, hands tied.

13
00:00:19,429 --> 00:00:20,649
His name is Sinon.

14
00:00:20,649 --> 00:00:22,390
Sobbing, he swears: It's a gift for

15
00:00:22,390 --> 00:00:23,050
Athena.

16
00:00:23,050 --> 00:00:24,170
If it enters your city,

17
00:00:24,170 --> 00:00:25,050
Troy can never fall.

18
00:00:25,050 --> 00:00:26,769
That's why they built it too big

19
00:00:26,769 --> 00:00:27,789
for your gates.

20
00:00:27,789 --> 00:00:29,690
Right on cue, two giant sea serpents

21
00:00:29,690 --> 00:00:31,629
crawl out of the ocean and strangle

22
00:00:31,629 --> 00:00:32,630
Laocoön.

23
00:00:32,630 --> 00:00:34,629
Message received: the horse is sacred.

24
00:00:34,780 --> 00:00:35,600
So how do you get a horse

25
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:37,240
through a gate it doesn't fit?

26
00:00:37,240 --> 00:00:39,500
The Trojans tear down their own walls.

27
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:42,299
Princess Cassandra screams, There are soldiers inside!

28
00:00:42,299 --> 00:00:43,479
Nobody believes her.

29
00:00:43,479 --> 00:00:45,960
She's literally cursed so nobody ever will.

30
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:47,859
That night, Helen circles the horse,

31
00:00:47,859 --> 00:00:49,960
imitating the voices of the soldiers' wives.

32
00:00:49,960 --> 00:00:51,539
One soldier is about to answer,

33
00:00:51,539 --> 00:00:53,560
until Odysseus clamps a hand over his

34
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:54,179
mouth.

35
00:00:54,179 --> 00:00:55,939
At midnight, Sinon opens the hatch.

36
00:00:55,939 --> 00:00:57,140
The soldiers open the gates,

37
00:00:57,140 --> 00:00:58,299
and the fleet that was hiding behind

38
00:00:58,299 --> 00:00:59,719
an island sails back.

39
00:00:59,969 --> 00:01:01,670
For ten years, the Greeks couldn't break

40
00:01:01,670 --> 00:01:02,530
those walls.

41
00:01:02,530 --> 00:01:03,729
The Trojans did it themselves,

42
00:01:03,729 --> 00:01:05,090
in one afternoon.

